3. INFRINGEMENT AND CIVIL ENFORCEMENT

A person who violates an exclusive right of the copyright owner is an infringer
under 17 U.S.C. § 501, subject to all applicable defenses, limitations, and
exceptions in Title 17.

GlacierEQ expressly reserves every remedy available under law, including, where
applicable:

- temporary and permanent injunctive relief under 17 U.S.C. § 502;
- impoundment and disposition of infringing articles under 17 U.S.C. § 503;
- actual damages and infringer's profits under 17 U.S.C. § 504(a)-(b);
- statutory damages under 17 U.S.C. § 504(c) when legally available, including
