- costs and reasonable attorney's fees under 17 U.S.C. § 505 when legally
  available and awarded by the court.

Nothing in this notice guarantees any particular remedy or outcome. Availability
of statutory damages and attorney's fees depends on the registration and timing
requirements of 17 U.S.C. § 412 and other applicable law.

4. REGISTRATION AND ENFORCEMENT PRESERVATION

For United States works, 17 U.S.C. § 411 governs registration prerequisites for
civil infringement actions. GlacierEQ reserves the right to register protected
works with the United States Copyright Office and to supplement, update, or
record ownership information as appropriate.

Where timely registration requirements are satisfied, 17 U.S.C. §§ 412, 504,
and 505 may permit statutory damages and attorney's fees. Under 17 U.S.C.
§ 504(c), statutory damages may range from $750 to $30,000 per infringed work as
the court considers just, and may be increased up to $150,000 per work where
willful infringement is proven, subject to the statute and the facts of the case.

